00:06:28.417 --> 00:06:31.600
The answer is A: community stewardship.

80
00:06:33.117 --> 00:06:38.007
According to the text, when was Angkor inscribed on the World Heritage List?

81
00:06:38.307 --> 00:06:45.896
A, 1979. B, 1992. C, 2008.

82
00:06:49.883 --> 00:06:53.334
The answer is B: 1992.

83
00:06:54.850 --> 00:07:00.753
Now it's your turn. Part one: How can Cambodia balance tourism and heritage protection?

84
00:07:06.053 --> 00:07:12.511
Part two: Propose two measures, explain their benefits and one possible conflict.

85
00:07:18.811 --> 00:07:31.587
By limiting visitor numbers at fragile temples and training local guides, Cambodia could protect sites while creating jobs. However, limiting visitors might reduce income for some businesses in the short term.

86
00:07:31.887 --> 00:07:34.177
That is a well-argued answer!

87
00:07:35.183 --> 00:07:40.796
Great work today! You learned eight new words and future perfect continuous (mastery).

88
00:07:41.096 --> 00:07:46.361
Today's value is love of country. Love and take care of Cambodia.

89
00:07:46.661 --> 00:07:50.532
See you in Unit forty-three. Goodbye!

90
00:07:50.832 --> 00:07:53.995
Thank you, Ms. Sarah! Bye, everyone!

